# Strategy template catalog (LEAN + community)

Phase 7 of the multi-tenant rollout. Hard rule 35 in
[AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) is the source of truth.

## Ingestion

- Read-only strategy templates land in the polymorphic
  [`resources`](mdc:aqp/persistence/models_resources.py) table with
  ``resource_type='strategy_template'``,
  ``owner_scope_kind='organization'``, and ``visibility='org'``.
- The QuantConnect LEAN ingester
  ([`scripts/ingest_lean_templates.py`](mdc:scripts/ingest_lean_templates.py))
  is idempotent: re-running with a newer LEAN revision overwrites
  the matching rows in place + emits a lineage event.
- New template sources (community frameworks, internal references)
  add an ingester next to ``ingest_lean_templates.py`` that follows
  the same upsert pattern.

## Translation

- LEAN -> ``FrameworkAlgorithm`` skeleton lives in
  [`aqp/strategies/lean/translator.py`](mdc:aqp/strategies/lean/translator.py).
  The mapping is pure-Python AST rewriting + a small lookup table
  (`_METHOD_REMAP`, `_CTX_API_REMAP`, `_INDICATOR_NAMES`).
- Unmapped LEAN API calls become ``# TODO(lean-translate)``
  comments retaining the original line — never silently dropped.
- Cloning a template through
  [`data.strategies.templates.clone_to_workspace`](mdc:aqp/data/mcp/tools/strategies.py)
  or ``POST /strategies/templates/clone`` writes a new Resource owned
  by the calling user + a `resource_relations.relation='translated_from'`
  edge back to the source. The ownership graph projector picks the
  edge up automatically.

## Agent surface

- Agents browse + clone via the
  [`data.strategies.templates.*`](mdc:aqp/data/mcp/tools/strategies.py)
  MCP tools. The clone tool is the only mutator in the family
  (scope `data:write`).
- The strategy palette in the Vite frontend reads
  ``GET /strategies/templates`` and ``GET
  /strategies/templates/{id}`` so users + agents see the same
  catalog.

## Don't list

- Don't hand-write strategy template rows — go through the
  ingester (existing) or the agent surface (clone tool).
- Don't store a LEAN template under a different ``resource_type``;
  the strategy_templates cache category filters on the discriminator.
- Don't translate inside the ingester — translation is the user's
  opt-in choice at clone time.

